# Normalise line endings in the repository; check out native on each platform.
* text=auto

# Explicitly binary - never touched by EOL normalisation.
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.joblib binary
*.pkl   binary
*.parquet binary
# Hashed in the manifest. Git would auto-detect it as binary from its NUL
# bytes, but auto-detection is a heuristic and these bytes must never change.
*.npy   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated model artifacts: never line-ending converted.
#
# The manifest records a SHA-256 of every artifact and the loader re-hashes them
# on startup. Line-ending normalisation rewrites those bytes at checkout time, so
# a file written on Windows (CRLF) hashes differently after a Linux checkout (LF)
# and the integrity check correctly reports it as changed - which is what broke
# the first Streamlit Community Cloud deployment.
#
# The .parquet/.joblib/.npy artifacts were already safe because they are marked
# binary above. These are the text ones.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models/*.json                  -text
artifacts/production/*.json    -text
